<item>
            <title>[LU-20292] Fix Lustre kernel rpms naming</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20292</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;It looks like Lustre kernel rpms naming could be improved to better reflect the baseline kernel version, e.g.&lt;br/&gt;
baseline kernel-4.18.0-553.117.1.el8_10.src.rpm Lustre kernel-4.18.0-553.117.1.el8_lustre.x86_64.rpm&lt;br/&gt;
-&amp;gt; should be kernel-4.18.0-553.117.1.el8_10_lustre.x86_64.rpm&lt;br/&gt;
baseline kernel-5.14.0-503.40.1.el9_5.src.rpm Lustre kernel-5.14.0-503.40.1_lustre.el9.x86_64.rpm&lt;br/&gt;
-&amp;gt; should be kernel-5.14.0-503.40.1.el9_5_lustre.x86_64.rpm&lt;br/&gt;
baseline kernel-6.12.0-124.49.1.el10_1.src.rpm Lustre kernel-6.12.0-124.49.1_lustre.el10.x86_64.rpm&lt;br/&gt;
-&amp;gt; should be kernel-6.12.0-124.49.1.el10_1_lustre.x86_64.rpm&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is important for tools that check the kernel version and make string version comparisons (&quot;is the kernel version at least xxx?&quot;).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
